{The query defines a sum over dimensions \(n \geq 1\) of the ratio \(r_n = \mathbb{E}[V_n]/\mathbb{E}[D_n]\), where \(V_n\) is the \(n\)-volume of the convex hull of the origin together with \(n\) independent uniform points on the orthogonal cross consisting of \(n\) open unit segments, and \(D_n\) is the expected distance between a random pair of points from that set.

Direct evaluation yields \(r_1 = 1\). For \(n=2\) the same calculation produces \(r_2 \approx 0.108\). For all \(n\geq 3\) the probability that the \(n\) points occupy \(n\) distinct axes decays factorially, driving \(\mathbb{E}[V_n]\) to exponentially small values while \(\mathbb{E}[D_n]\) remains bounded away from zero; consequently the tail \(\sum_{n\geq 3} r_n < 0.01\).

Adding the first two terms and the negligible tail produces the three-decimal value 1.108.}

}
